Chapter: TagEqual
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 tag-equal answers whether two variant values carry the same
 constructor tag without inspecting fields. Both same-tag and
 different-tag pairs are pinned, over a local sum with nullary and
 fielded constructors and over the foreword Maybe, and the type
 forces both arguments to one scrutinee type.

Section: Types

  Shape =
   | Dot
   | Circle (Integer)
   | Rect (Integer) (Integer)

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("a=" & show (tag-equal (Circle 3) (Circle 9)))
    print-line-uni ("b=" & show (tag-equal (Circle 3) (Rect 1 2)))
    print-line-uni ("c=" & show (tag-equal Dot Dot))
    print-line-uni ("d=" & show (tag-equal Dot (Circle 1)))
    print-line-uni ("e=" & show (tag-equal (Just 5) (Just 7)))
    print-line-uni ("f=" & show (tag-equal (Just 5) None))
  end
